# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Line-ending protection for preserved source material.
#
# core.autocrlf is enabled on at least one founder machine. Without
# these rules, Git would check preserved files out with CRLF endings,
# which would:
#   - break byte-for-byte fidelity with the delivered packages, and
#   - make `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt` FAIL inside
#     archive/raw-migration-source/instagram_media_supplemental_artifacts/
#
# `-text` disables all line-ending conversion, so these files are
# stored and checked out exactly as delivered on every platform.
#
# DO NOT REMOVE. The archive's provenance guarantee depends on it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Pristine migration source — everything, unconditionally
archive/raw-migration-source/** -text

# Recovered historical documents, preserved verbatim elsewhere in the tree.
# These are byte-identical copies of the archived originals; they must stay
# that way so `diff` against the archive keeps passing.
strategy/research/INITIAL_STRATEGIC_AUDIT.md                             -text
strategy/research/PHASE_1_PHASE_2_REPORT.md                              -text
strategy/historical/STRATEGY_EVOLUTION.md                                -text
strategy/historical/HISTORICAL_PRICE_MENU.md                             -text
experiment/historical-48-post-design/REVIVAL_EXPERIMENT_FINAL_LOCK.md    -text
experiment/historical-48-post-design/PATCH_AND_FREEZE_48_POST_MATRIX.md  -text
experiment/historical-48-post-design/FINAL_METHODOLOGY_PATCH_MATRIX_FROZEN.md -text

# Evidence screenshots — binary, never converted or diffed as text
*.jpeg binary
*.jpg  binary
*.zip  binary

# Note: authored documents (README, PROJECT_STATE, DECISIONS, HANDOFF,
# ROADMAP, CLAUDE.md, and the directory index files) are deliberately NOT
# listed. They are ordinary project docs and may follow platform defaults.
